part.text:
We need to add sounds. Likely use Web Audio API or HTML5 audio elements. Add background music and sound effects for thrust, collision, etc. Since we cannot see HTML, but can create audio elements via JS. We'll load sounds via URLs; maybe we can embed base64 data URIs. Simpler: create Audio objects with source files assumed to exist (e.g., 'thrust.wav', 'explosion.wav', 'bgm.mp3'). Use play on events: ship movement maybe thrust sound loop, collision sound, maybe score beep. We'll edit game.js to load sounds at start, play bgMusic loop, play thrust sound when moving, stop when not, play explosion on collision.

Implement with minimal changes. Need to ensure audio files are referenced; if not present, will error but fine.

Proceed to edit: add audio loading after canvas setup. Add variables: bgMusic = new Audio('bgm.mp3'); bgMusic.loop = true; bgMusic.volume=0.3; bgMusic.play();

thrustSound = new Audio('thrust.wav'); thrustSound.loop = true; thrustSound.volume=0.5;

explosionSound = new Audio('explosion.wav'); explosionSound.volume=0.7;

In updateShip, after computing movement, if any direction pressed, if not already playing thrustSound, play; else pause.

In collision detection, when collision true, play explosionSound.

Add logic to avoid multiple calls.

Implement via new variables, maybe using a flag.

Proceed to edit.

